{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017VpBLgd8wjh8vSngcRRrp7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd074-sha224sum\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sha224sum: Compute and Check SHA-224 Message Digests\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships shasum -a 224 rather than sha224sum; the invocation differs from GNU\n6\t  sha224sum. Scripts that generate or verify SHA-224 checksums using the GNU format\n7\t  must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew\n8\t  GNU reference binary (gsha224sum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag\n9\t  combinations, using crypto/sha256 (sha256.New224) from the Go standard library,\n10\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Compute SHA-224 digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gsha224sum behavior.\n14\t  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n15\t  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), and --tag output format flags.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Digest computation\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must compute the SHA-224 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"SHA224 (FILENAME) = HASH\".\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the SHA-224 digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Binary and text mode flags\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\".\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n47\t\n48\t  R4:\n49\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R4.1:\n52\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n53\t      - R4.2:\n54\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n55\t      - R4.3:\n56\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n57\t\n58\tnon_goals:\n59\t  - cmd/sha224sum does not implement HMAC-SHA224 or keyed variants.\n60\t  - cmd/sha224sum does not implement SHA-256; it computes SHA-224 only.\n61\t\n62\tpackage_contract:\n63\t  imports:\n64\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\n65\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n66\t\n67\tacceptance_criteria:\n68\t  - id: AC1\n69\t    criterion: \"sha224sum on a known file produces the correct SHA-224 hash in GNU format, matching gsha224sum.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R1.3\n74\t      - R1.4\n75\t  - id: AC2\n76\t    criterion: \"sha224sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n77\t    traces:\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R4.1\n82\t      - R4.2\n83\t      - R4.3\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"sha224sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R1.4\n88\t      - R2.1\n89\t      - R2.2\n90\t      - R4.1\n91\t      - R4.2\n92\t      - R4.3\n93\t  - id: AC4\n94\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsha224sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n95\t    traces:\n96\t      - R1.1\n97\t      - R1.2\n98\t      - R1.3\n99\t      - R1.4\n100\t  - id: AC5\n101\t    criterion: \"cmd/sha224sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n102\t    traces:\n103\t      - R1.1\n104\t      - R1.2\n105\t      - R1.3\n106\t      - R1.4\n107\t      - R2.1\n108\t      - R2.2\n109\t      - R2.3\n110\t      - R3.1\n111\t      - R3.2\n112\t      - R4.1\n113\t      - R4.2\n114\t      - R4.3\n115\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017ZGcwTJagEyr2Yjc3N3SCA","session_id":"bf4a14e2-8432-40d3-927b-e04343b7db02","uuid":"1f08cbf8-b214-40a5-b05c-9b6aef493252","timestamp":"2026-05-23T00:33:04.320Z"}
