{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ZGcwTJagEyr2Yjc3N3SCA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I've successfully read all the files. Here's the full contents of each:\n\n## 1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd074-sha224sum.yaml\n\n**R4.3 Requirement:**\nLine 55-56: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\"\n\n**Acceptance Criteria (AC2, AC3, AC4, AC5 all trace to R4.3):**\n- AC2 (lines 75-83): \"sha224sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n- AC3 (lines 84-92): \"sha224sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n- AC4 (lines 93-99): \"Differential test against gsha224sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n- AC5 (lines 100-114): \"cmd/sha224sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n\n## 2. cmd/sha224sum/main.go\n\nFull implementation present (172 lines total). Key points:\n- Uses `sha256.New224` for SHA-224 computation (line 45)\n- Installs SIGPIPE handler at startup (line 41)\n- Supports all flags: --binary, --text, --tag, --check, --warn, --quiet, --status, --zero\n- Delegates digest computation to `hashutil.DigestFiles` and verification to `hashutil.VerifyChecksums`\n- Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 on errors or verification failures\n\n## 3. cmd/sha224sum/sha224sum_test.go\n\nFull test implementation present (316 lines). Contains:\n- **TestDiff()**: Differential test against `gsha224sum` with 35 test cases covering:\n  - R1.1-R1.4: Digest computation scenarios\n  - R2.1-R2.3: Checksum verification with flags (--check, --warn, --quiet, --status)\n  - R3.1-R3.2: Binary/text/tag format modes\n  - R4.1-R4.2: Exit codes (0 and 1 scenarios)\n  \n- **TestSIGPIPE()**: Tests graceful handling of SIGPIPE when stdout is closed early (lines 274-303)\n\nTest utilities use `testutils.BuildBinary()`, `testutils.RunDiffTests()`, and normalization functions to discard stderr